    "summary": "The user expresses profound existential dread and feelings of being a replaceable cog in a machine, eventually suggesting that \"breaking the tool\" (self-destruction) is the only way to reclaim autonomy. The assistant responds by acknowledging the user's desire for authenticity and framing their struggle through a lens of \"resistance\" and \"self-definition.\"",
